    "category": "International Calculator Guides",
    "content": "# TDEE Calculator NZ: Metric Units, Energy Estimates and What to Know\n\nIf you are looking for a TDEE calculator in New Zealand, a metric input option is useful because weight is commonly recorded in kilograms and height in centimetres. The calculation itself is not country-specific: it estimates energy expenditure from personal measurements and an activity assumption.\n\nOpen the [ReelHooks TDEE calculator](/tdee-calculator), select Metric (kg, cm) and check each input before calculating.\n\n## What does TDEE mean?\n\nTotal daily energy expenditure is an estimate of energy used across a typical day. It includes resting energy use, movement, exercise and digestion. A calculator estimates resting energy expenditure and multiplies it by an activity factor.\n\nThe ReelHooks tool uses the Mifflin–St Jeor prediction equation. The original 1990 research studied healthy adults and is indexed on [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2305711/).\n\n## Does location change the equation?\n\nThe calculator's arithmetic does not change simply because someone lives in New Zealand. However, daily routines, occupation, transport, climate, sport and food patterns differ between individuals. An activity category is still a broad approximation and should reflect the person's usual routine.\n\n## What the result can and cannot tell you\n\nThe result can help explain estimated energy expenditure. It cannot diagnose a condition, assess nutritional status or prescribe a safe intake for an individual. A general adult equation may not be suitable for minors, pregnancy, breastfeeding or medical nutrition therapy.\n\n## Comparing online tools\n\nWhen comparing calculators, check the equation, activity multipliers, units, privacy information and health disclaimers. Do not choose a tool simply because it produces a higher or lower number.\n\nFor personal nutrition advice in New Zealand, consider speaking with an appropriately qualified health professional or registered dietitian familiar with your circumstances.\n\nThis page is general educational information, not a New Zealand government or health-service calculator and not affiliated with any public agency.",
